884 0 obj
<<
/Title (The experiments confirm the central pattern of instance-based learning: local methods are flexible but depend strongly on distance geometry, the neighbourhood size, bandwidth or the quality of stored cases. Standardising Q2 features improves validation accuracy, irrelevant dimensions harm neighbour contrast, and Q7 train-only feature filtering recovers that loss. Q3 shows that local regression bandwidth balances flexibility against stability and prediction expense. Q4 demonstrates that a small nonlinear RBF feature map can linearise XOR and fit noisy crescent patterns. Q5 adds case revision and controlled retention, while Q6 quantifies the storage and prediction-latency costs of storing examples versus fitting a compact eager model.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 734 0 R
/First 1051 0 R
/Last 1051 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
